---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '../site.config';
---

<Base title="About" description={`What ${siteConfig.name} is, who it is for, and how it is made.`}>
  <article class="wrap prose">
    <p class="kicker"><b>About</b></p>
    <h1>Small tools for people who build.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      {siteConfig.name} is a free collection of references and utilities for Power Apps and Power Automate makers.
    </p>
    <p>
      It started as a personal cheat sheet: the formulas I kept looking up, written the way I wish they had been explained
      to me, with an example I could paste straight in. It grew into a site so others could use it too.
    </p>

    <h2>Who it is for</h2>
    <p>
      Citizen developers, analysts and pro developers who work in the Power Platform and want a quick answer without
      opening five tabs.
    </p>

    <h2>How it is made</h2>
    <p>
      The site is built with Astro and React and is published as static files. There is no database, no account system
      and no tracking of what you type.
    </p>

    <h2>Corrections and ideas</h2>
    <p>
      Found a mistake, or want a formula or tool added? <a href={siteConfig.feedbackUrl} rel="noopener">Open an issue</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
